---
id: system-improvement
title: Diagnose, change, review
purpose: A coding mission with the SDLC cognition profile; one agent diagnoses a wrong behaviour, a second proposes the change test-first, a human reviews.
use_when: The user names a behaviour that is wrong today, how to observe it and what must keep working.
produces: The text outputs `diagnose.diagnosis` and `change.change_report` (the change as a diff and the tests that ran), then one REVIEW Human Task at `review`. Approving it accepts the mission; nothing is merged or published.
slots:
  application_id:
    description: This server's application id (the start page names it).
    example: demo-app
  mission_key:
    description: "A stable slug for the mission: lower case letters, digits, `-` or `_`."
    example: system-improvement
  title:
    description: A one-line title.
    example: Fix the failing parser test
  request:
    description: The user's request in their own words, verbatim, one line.
    example: The parser rejects a manifest that ends with a comment. Please fix it.
  question:
    description: One question you asked in the interview. Add one `answers` entry for each further question.
    example: What must keep working?
  answer:
    description: The user's answer to that question, verbatim, one line.
    example: Every other parser test, and manifests without comments must parse as before.
  done_means:
    description: What the user said finished looks like, verbatim, one line.
    example: The failing test is green and I can read the diff in a minute.
  out_of_scope:
    description: What the user ruled out, verbatim, one line. Delete the `out_of_scope` entry when they ruled out nothing.
    example: No refactoring of the parser.
  goal:
    description: The behaviour that is wrong today and how to observe it, one line.
    example: The parser rejects a manifest with a trailing comment; reproduce it with the parser test and fix it.
  criterion:
    description: What must hold after the change, one line.
    example: The failing test passes, every other test still passes and the diff is minimal.
  repository_url:
    description: The repository the change lands in (https or ssh).
    example: "https://example.invalid/org/repository.git"
  repository_ref:
    description: The branch or commit to start from.
    example: main
  model_profile:
    description: A Model Profile the lane routes (topic `models`).
    example: producer.default
  sandbox_profile:
    description: A sandbox profile bound on this installation (topic `manifest`).
    example: research.standard
  budget_usd:
    description: The ceiling on model spend in US dollars, a number.
    example: "3"
  reviewer:
    description: Who resolves the review; an actor id, or a reviewer role such as `owner`. Only that actor, or a principal holding `reviewer:<role>`, can.
    example: owner
notes:
  - Compiles against the seeded catalog; not yet proven by a run.
  - On the `deep_agents` lane the agent works in its sandbox and fetches the repository itself. Mission Control checks out `workspace.repo` only on the repository-bound lanes (topic `lanes`), so the sandbox must be allowed to reach the repository.
  - The `change` stage reads the accepted diagnosis through its `from` binding. A start is refused with `dependent_inputs_unavailable` where the installation composes no trusted settlement.
  - The `brief` block is the interview's result in the user's words. Every node is told the purpose, the request, what done means, what it was given and each criterion whose `evidence` names an output it owes, so an `instruction` holds the task alone.
---
manifest: mission/v2
mission:
  key: {{mission_key}}
  application: {{application_id}}
  title: >-
    {{title}}
  description: >-
    {{goal}}
  brief:
    purpose: system
    request: >-
      {{request}}
    answers:
      - question: >-
          {{question}}
        answer: >-
          {{answer}}
    done_means: >-
      {{done_means}}
    out_of_scope:
      - >-
        {{out_of_scope}}
  goals:
    - key: improvement
      description: >-
        {{goal}}
      importance: primary
      objectives:
        - key: diagnose_fault
          description: Reproduce the behaviour and name its cause with evidence.
        - key: make_change
          description: Change the code test-first and report the diff and the tests that ran.
      criteria:
        - key: change_reviewed
          description: >-
            {{criterion}}
          evidence: [diagnosis, change_report]
          acceptance:
            human: review_accept
  environment:
    lane: deep_agents
    model:
      profile: {{model_profile}}
    sandbox:
      profile: {{sandbox_profile}}
    workspace:
      repo:
        url: {{repository_url}}
        ref: {{repository_ref}}
    plugins:
      - pin: plugin.cognition-sdlc@latest
        as: sdlc
    capabilities:
      - pin: tool.knowledge-submit-output@latest
        kind: tool
        as: submit_output
    budget:
      usd: {{budget_usd}}
      tokens: 800000
      wall_clock: 1h
      tool_calls: 120
    governors:
      depth: 1
      fan_out: 1
      iterations: 1
      patience: 1
    side_effects: [read_only, workspace_write]
  program:
    key: root
    behavior: stage_graph
    objectives: [improvement]
    nodes:
      - key: diagnose
        behavior: agent_executor
        objectives: [diagnose_fault]
        environment:
          budget:
            tokens: 300000
            tool_calls: 50
        instruction: >-
          {{goal}}
          Work in {{repository_url}} at {{repository_ref}}. Reproduce the behaviour and find
          its cause. Submit the diagnosis as "diagnose.diagnosis" with the submit_output tool,
          as one inline text item.
        outputs:
          - name: diagnosis
            form: text
            media_type: text/plain
      - key: change
        behavior: agent_executor
        objectives: [make_change]
        environment:
          budget:
            tokens: 450000
            tool_calls: 65
        inputs:
          - name: diagnosis
            from: diagnose.diagnosis
            expand: materialize
        instruction: >-
          Make the change the diagnosis you received calls for, test-first, in
          {{repository_url}} at {{repository_ref}}. Submit the change report as
          "change.change_report" with the submit_output tool, as one inline text item holding
          the diff and each test command with its result.
        outputs:
          - name: change_report
            form: text
            media_type: text/plain
      - key: review
        behavior: human_gate
        objectives: [improvement]
        depends_on: [change]
        task:
          kind: REVIEW
          prompt: >-
            {{criterion}}
          reviewers: [{{reviewer}}]
          packet: [diagnose.diagnosis, change.change_report]
          on_timeout: keep_waiting
  controls:
    commands_allowed: [pause, resume, cancel, queue_instruction, add_context]
